```

Core trait:

```rust
pub trait SimCore {
    fn new(cfg: SimConfig) -> Self where Self: Sized;
    fn tick(&mut self, cmds: &[Command]) -> Frame;   // exactly one per call
    fn head(&self) -> &Frame;                        // latest committed
    fn frame_at(&self, t: Tick) -> Option<Arc<WorldState>>; // ring buffer lookup
    fn to_bytes(&self) -> Vec<u8>;                   // canonical
    fn from_bytes(&mut self, b: &[u8]) -> Result<(), LoadError>;
    fn digest(&self) -> [u8;32];
}
```

Renderer trait:

```rust
pub trait Renderer {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str;
    fn on_commit(&mut self, f: &Frame);       // store refs, spawn local fx from events
    fn present(&mut self, out: &mut dyn PresentTarget, alpha: Alpha);
    fn last_verified_tick(&self) -> Tick;
}
```

Alpha: computed by shell as acc/DT in [0,1).

Asset indirection:

```rust
pub type AssetId = SmolStr; // logical: "sfx/laser", "mesh/unit_tank"
```

Core never holds GPU/text/font handles.

Presentation extras: core may include `pub presentation: PresentationHints` inside WorldState? Careful: hints like facing direction are gameplay-derived and fine; camera shake amounts etc. should be events. Keep hints minimal: focus point, round timer display value.

Bus/shell:

```rust
pub struct Shell<C: SimCore> {
    core: C,
    renderers: Vec<Box<dyn Renderer>>,
    recorder: Option<Recorder>,
    verifier: Option<TwinVerifier>,
    acc: Duration, dt: Duration,
}
impl Shell { pub fn run(...) }
```

Verification:

```rust
pub trait Verifier {
    fn on_commit(&mut self, f: &Frame);
    fn report(&self) -> VerifyReport;
}
// Twin: second SimCore instance (possibly other-language via FFI) fed identical command slices; compares digests each tick.
```

Canonical encoding rules: little-endian, fields in schema order, no padding, strings length-prefixed UTF-8, enums as u16 discriminant + payload, entities ascending id, skip nothing. Hash = BLAKE3(canonical_bytes || schema_version || tick).

Determinism rules list:
- Fixed timestep only; core has no clock.
- All randomness via `Rng::stream(id).next_u64()`; streams seeded from `cfg.seed ^ stream_id`; counters stored in state (so snapshots reproduce).
- Iteration order: ascending EntityId always; collections are Vec/BTreeMap only.
- No floats in sim; conversions to float happen in renderers only.
- No global/thread-local state; no allocation-address-dependent behavior; no HashMap iteration.
- Commands applied in canonical order: sort by (due, player, seq); duplicates dropped by (player,seq).
- Input delay: commands scheduled for tick T must be known before T begins (lockstep) or use rollback (out of scope here, mention hook).

Rollback hook optional: `fn resimulate(&mut self, from: Tick, cmds: &Timeline)` — mention as extension.

Interpolation contract: renderer interpolates only between frame[tick-1].state and frame[tick].state for matching EntityId; missing prior → snap; destroyed → use tombstone (last transform retained one frame in a side map built from events).

Text renderer example mapping to show agnosticism: archetype table → glyph string; 3D: archetype → mesh AssetId → loaded glTF; 2D: sprite sheet index. Same Frame drives all three; each asserts digest match.

Main loop code with accumulator, catch-up cap, panic on spiral.

Also multi-rate presentation: present called at display rate (e.g., 144Hz) with alpha; commits at 60Hz.

Recorder format: header{schema_version, seed, cfg_hash} then per-tick command batches; replay = new core + feed batches; compare digest chain.

Failure handling: on digest mismatch, verifier emits first_bad_tick; debug tooling: bisect entities by comparing canonical dumps.

I think also worth specifying the exact publication semantics: Frame is Arc, immutable forever ("committed" = frozen + hashed). Renderers hold Arc clones; shell guarantees at most one pending un-presented frame per renderer or drop policy (renderers may skip frames; they must still verify digests of frames they see; skipped frames fine because next frame carries prev_digest chain enabling gap detection: renderer tracks expected prev_digest).

Gap detection detail: each Frame has prev_digest; a renderer that saw tick n with digest d expects next seen frame to have prev_digest == d OR tick jump recorded (if it intentionally skips). If mismatch → desync alert. Nice.

Let me also define PresentTarget minimal: renderers write to their own backends actually; simpler: present(&mut self, alpha) and renderer owns its window/canvas. Keep `out` abstract or drop it. I'll give renderer ownership of its sink, constructed externally.

Config:

```rust
pub struct SimConfig {
    pub seed: u64,
    pub tick_rate: u32,          // e.g., 60
    pub players: Vec<PlayerId>,
    pub rules: RulesBlob,        // versioned tuning data, content-hashed
}
```

Include cfg_hash in digest chain? Include schema_version + rules_hash in header of digest computation. Yes: digest = H(domain_tag, schema_version, rules_hash, tick, prev_digest, canonical_state_excluding_tick?) — careful recursion: state includes tick; fine, just hash whole canonical state including tick, plus prev_digest chained to bind history. Chaining binds command history implicitly too (since state depends on commands). Good.

Edge: initial frame tick 0 published at start (commit of initial state) so renderers have something to show and baseline digest.

